-- title:
--   Ordinary Frobenius scalar is a unit root of X²-Tₚ X+p
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and $\bar\rho$ a residual representation of $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a two-dimensional space over the residue field of $\mathcal O$, factoring through a finite level, absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure) and ordinary at $p$ in the sense that for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit there is a line spanned by the first vector of some basis which is stable under the decomposition group and modulo which inertia acts trivially. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $N$ be prime to $p$ with all its prime divisors in $S$ and with the cusp forms of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ spanned by those with integral $q$-expansion, and let $r$ be a prime not dividing $Np$. Fix $H_0\le(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ together with the level datum $h_{10}$ asserting $Nr\mid Nr$, $1\mid 1$ and that $H_0$ maps into the full group, i.e. $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)\le\Gamma_0(Nr)$ at degeneracy parameter $1$. Let $\theta_0:\mathbb T^S(N)\to\mathcal O/\mathfrak m$ be a character of the anemic Hecke algebra (generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ outside $S$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$ one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta_0(T_\ell)X+\ell$, and let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the localisation $\mathbb T^S(N)_{\theta_0}$ to $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathbb T_0$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra acting on $H^1(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr),\mathcal O)=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$ compatibly with $\mathcal O$, and $cd_0$ corner data for it (an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T_0$, an index, and a level pairing on the corresponding corner ring and corner submodule), with an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e_0$ from the corner ring onto $\mathbb T^S(N)_{\theta_0}$ such that for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nr$ the element $e_0^{-1}(T_\ell)$ acts on the corner module as the cohomological Hecke operator $T_\ell$ on $H^1(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr),\mathcal O)$. Let $t_p$ be a unit of the corner ring acting there as the cohomological $T_p$, assume the submodule of the corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0)$ is non-zero, and assume every class in the corner submodule lies in the image, under pullback along $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)\le\Gamma_0(Nr)$, of the parabolic homomorphisms on $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ (those vanishing on elements of trace square $4$). Finally let $\rho'$ be a two-dimensional adically continuous representation over $\mathcal O$ with $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho'(\sigma))=X^2-\pi_{T_0}(T_\ell)X+\ell$ at Frobenii at all primes $\ell\nmid N$ outside $S$, let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $p$, let $L$ be a line in $\rho'.V$ spanned by the first vector of some basis, stable under the decomposition group at $P$ and with inertia acting trivially modulo $L$, and let $\alpha\in\mathcal O$ be such that every Frobenius at $p$ in the decomposition group acts by $\alpha$ modulo $L$. Then $\alpha$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ and $\alpha^2-\pi_{T_0}(e_0(t_p))\,\alpha+p=0$.
--
--   This identifies the scalar by which Frobenius at $p$ acts on the unramified quotient of an ordinary $p$-adic representation as the unit root of the Hecke polynomial $X^2-a_pX+p$, with $a_p$ read off from the corner element $t_p$ through the $\mathcal O$-point $\pi_{T_0}$; the parabolicity hypothesis on the corner is what allows $\pi_{T_0}(e_0(t_p))$ to be matched with the $p$-th coefficient of a newform via Eichler–Shimura. It feeds the construction of the level-raising rung at the residue characteristic, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_heckeModule_rung_at_residueChar_unitRoot_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_heckeModule_rung_at_residueChar_unitRoot_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_not_cube_dvd).
